  5 Aug 2026 (New York run) - two CORRECTIONS to entries below, both found only
  because the NY import forced a same-address diff. Note WHY they were invisible
  before: every NY legacy record stores an EMPTY address, so a scan over stored
  values sees nothing. These addresses exist ONLY here, and only at render time.
  A stored-data scan structurally cannot find a collision in this file.

  1. Vitor Shaolin BJJ NYC: was 220 E 86th St. That is Modern Martial Arts NYC
     Upper Eastside, which is now imported as its own record - two records would
     have rendered at one address. The school this record actually points at
     (bjjnewyorkcity.com) trades as NYC BJJ Academy and its own footer gives
     780 8th Avenue, New York, NY 10036. The two businesses are co-branded and
     share the UES site, but 780 8th Ave is this record's own location.
     Corrected to 780 8th Ave, which also keeps the city (New York) truthful.

  2. Kioto Brazilian Jiu Jitsu: entry REMOVED, not corrected. It read
     1786 3rd Ave, which is Next Evolution Martial Arts' address - the line
     immediately below still carries it correctly. The Kioto record was
     back-filled from a MatMade listing (Kioto Brazilian Jiu Jitsu / NEMMAA)
     that is really Next Evolution running a Kioto-affiliated program.
     The real Kioto is 96 Biltmore Ave, OAKDALE, and this record's city says
     New York. Per this file's own rule - skip when the address sits in a
     different city than our data records, because it produces a misleading
     map link - it gets no entry until the city is fixed by a snippet rewrite
     (backlog item 0c).
